--- /dev/null
+++ b/openspec/changes/archive/2026-11-20-fix-coupon-giveback-on-cancel/proposal.md
@@ -0,0 +1,26 @@
+## Why
+
+A customer placed an order with a single-use welcome code, cancelled it within the window, and the code was then refused as already used. The README says a cancelled order gives its single-use coupon back. `Orders.cancel` in `src/orders.ts` passes the customer name to `Coupons.giveBack`, which only releases the coupon when the id of the order that used it matches, so the coupon is never released.
+
+A second report says free shipping was not applied to goods of exactly €50.00. Investigation shows this is already fixed: `shippingCost` uses `goods >= 5000`, `openspec/specs/shipping` covers the boundary, and `test/orders.test.ts` has a test for exactly 5000 cents. No change is needed. A €4.90 charge can still be correct when goods come to €50.00 before a coupon or volume discount and fall below €50.00 after, since the README measures the goods after every discount.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- `Orders.cancel` gives the single-use coupon back by the id of the cancelled order, so the code can be used again.
+- A regression test covers place, cancel and re-place with the same single-use code.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+
+None.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+- `coupons`: adds the requirement that cancelling an order makes its single-use coupon usable again.
+
+## Impact
+
+- README business rules affected: "A single-use coupon can be used by one order only; if that order is cancelled, the coupon can be used again", and the cancellation rule that gives back the coupon. The README is already correct and is not edited.
+- Code: `src/orders.ts` (`cancel`). Tests: `test/orders.test.ts`.
+- Out of scope: the free-shipping threshold (already correct), shipping VAT, other coupon rules, and cancelling shipped orders.
